      "statement": "A 2-year-old boy presents with recurrent urinary tract infections, a weak urinary stream, and failure to thrive. A voiding cystourethrogram shows dilatation of the posterior urethra with a thickened bladder wall producing a keyhole appearance, consistent with posterior urethral valves. What is the appropriate management for this condition?",
