      "number": 53,
      "statement": "A 32-year-old woman presents with galactorrhea along with headaches and visual disturbances for several months. A urine pregnancy test is negative, and physical examination is unremarkable. MRI of the brain shows a large pituitary tumor, and the patient declines surgical management. Which medication is the most appropriate treatment option in this case?",
