      "answerText": "(C) 600 to mother, 1400 to ASHA",
      "explanation": "Under the Janani Suraksha Yojana (JSY), financial incentives are provided to promote institutional deliveries, especially in states with low institutional delivery rates. Madhya Pradesh is classified as a Low Performing State (LPS) under this scheme.\nIn urban areas of Low Performing States, the incentive distribution is structured differently between the mother and the Accredited Social Health Activist (ASHA) worker who motivates and assists the pregnant woman.\nAccording to JSY guidelines:\n1. The mother receives ₹600 as a cash incentive for delivering in a government or accredited health facility.\n2. The ASHA worker receives ₹1400, which includes compensation for identifying the pregnant woman, counseling her for institutional delivery, accompanying her to the health facility, and ensuring postnatal follow-up care.\nThe larger incentive for the ASHA worker reflects her key role in community mobilization, ensuring antenatal checkups, facilitating institutional delivery, and providing postnatal support.\nTherefore, for a woman living in an urban area of Madhya Pradesh who delivers in a healthcare institution after counseling by an ASHA worker, the entitlement is:\nMother – ₹600\nASHA – ₹1400\nHence, the correct answer is (C) 600 to mother, 1400 to ASHA.",
