      "number": 188,
      "statement": "A 30-year-old man involved in a road traffic accident is brought to the emergency department. Although his vital signs are stable, he is unable to pass urine, and blood is noted at the urethral meatus. A retrograde urethrogram (RGU) is performed and shows the findings illustrated below. Based on the clinical presentation and imaging, what is the most likely site of urethral injury?",
