      "statement": "A 56-year-old patient has experienced severe chest discomfort over the past 72 hours that is relieved by glyceryl trinitrate (GTN) spray. Investigations show normal troponin I levels, and the ECG demonstrates left ventricular hypertrophy with T-wave flattening. The patient is already taking statins, aspirin, and metoprolol 50 mg. What is the next best step in management?",
