      "explanation": "Obstetric history is recorded using the gravida and para system.\nGravida (G) refers to the total number of pregnancies a woman has had, regardless of the outcome, including the current pregnancy. Since she had one previous pregnancy and is currently pregnant, her gravida is 2 (G2).\nPara (P) refers to the number of pregnancies that have been carried to a viable gestational age (typically >20 weeks), not the number of fetuses delivered. A twin pregnancy counts as a single delivery event. Since she has had one previous pregnancy that resulted in a delivery, her para is 1 (P1). Therefore, her correct obstetric status is G2P1. The options G2P2 or G2P3 are incorrect as they wrongly count the number of babies instead of the number of pregnancies carried to viability.",
