      "number": 114,
      "statement": "Nosocomial infections are defined as infections that develop after how many hours of hospital admission?",
      "options": [
        "48 hrs",
        "72 hrs",
        "24 hrs",
        "50 hrs"
      ],
      "correct": "A",
      "answerText": "(A) 48 hrs",
      "explanation": "A nosocomial infection, also known as a hospital-acquired infection (HAI), is defined as an infection that is acquired in a hospital or other healthcare facility and was not present or incubating at the time of admission. To distinguish HAIs from community-acquired infections that may become apparent after admission, a standard time-based criterion is used. An infection is generally classified as nosocomial if it first appears 48 hours or more after hospital admission. This 48-hour window is considered sufficient time to exclude infections that were incubating upon arrival. The definition also includes infections that appear after discharge if they are related to the hospitalization or a procedure performed during the stay, as well as occupational infections among healthcare staff.",
